# Reproduction for bead inc-gatz: a creature that walks into a field whose
# effect enlarges it to a size with a FaceRadius is relinked at the wrong
# square (Thing::Move relinks after EV_FIELDON; Values.cpp:1798 PlaceNear moved
# it meanwhile). Needs the scratch module with tools/fixtures/inc-gatz-growth.irh
# appended (tools/check_inc_gatz.sh builds it).

@include chargen.keys
@until "HP:" ESC

w y
@choose "Ascend / Descend Depth"
"2" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC

w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
@until "HP:" ESC

# Lay plain ground ("Loose-Packed Earth": a dry, walkable terrain) under the
# player and the two squares east before staging, so the walk below cannot be
# blocked by whatever terrain the generator chose. On seed 1 depth 2 the
# player starts in deep water, and the deep-water handler (lib/dungeon.irh)
# aborts a move whenever the Swim check fails, so the earlier fixed walk out
# of the start square never reached the field on that terrain.
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
ENTER
@choose "Loose-Packed Earth"
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT ENTER
@choose "Loose-Packed Earth"
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT*2 ENTER
@choose "Loose-Packed Earth"

# Summon the growth archon two squares east. Its field (ADJUST_CIRC, radius
# 1) covers the square one east of the player, so stepping there enters it:
# that Thing::Move is the path whose relink the fix guards. Dump the screen
# while the "You swell enormously!" message is up, so the check can see the
# field was entered.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Celestials"
@choose "gatz growth archon"
RIGHT*2 ENTER
@dump:summoned

RIGHT
@dump:step1
@quit
